11
00:43:07,199 --> 00:43:13,199
Witchboard is a 1986 American supernatural horror film written and directed by Kevin Tenney in
his directorial debut, and starring Tawny Kitaen, Stephen Nichols, and Todd Allen.

12
00:47:02,399 --> 00:47:08,399
The plot centers on college student Linda Brewster who becomes entranced into using
her friend's Ouija board alone after it was left behind at her party.

13
00:50:57,599 --> 00:51:03,599
She is subsequently terrorized and eventually possessed by the spirit of malevolent serial
killer Carlos Malfeitor, who committed a series of axe murders in the 1930s.

14
00:54:52,799 --> 00:54:58,799
Tenney wrote the screenplay while a student at the University of Southern California, inspired
after attending a party in which a friend brought a Ouija board for partygoers to use.

15
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:54,000
The film focuses on the notion of "progressive entrapment," the process by which a malevolent entity or demon takes control of a human
being, a theme that was also touched on in The Exorcist (1973) after Regan MacNeil (Linda Blair) dabbles with a Ouija board.

16
01:02:43,199 --> 01:02:49,199
Filming took place in 1985 in Los Angeles, San Bernardino, and San Francisco.

17
01:06:38,399 --> 01:06:44,399
Cinema Group gave Witchboard a limited theatrical release in
the United States on New Year's Eve 1986.

18
01:10:33,599 --> 01:10:39,599
Following favorable box-office returns, the release was expanded in the spring of
1987, and the film went on to gross $7.4 million in the United States.

19
01:14:28,800 --> 01:14:34,800
Although the critical response to the film was largely unfavorable, it has attracted a cult following
since its release, and was subject to significant critical analysis by academic Carol J.

20
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
Clover in her 1992 non-fiction book, Men, Women, and Chain Saws.

21
01:22:19,199 --> 01:22:25,199
Two unrelated sequels, Witchboard 2: The Devil's Doorway and Witchboard III:
The Possession, were released in 1993 and 1995, respectively.

22
01:26:14,399 --> 01:26:20,399
A remake directed by Chuck Russell was released in 2024.

23
01:30:09,599 --> 01:30:15,599
The film explores themes of medium, possession, evil
spirit, psychic power, ouija board.

24
01:34:04,799 --> 01:34:10,799
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
